A closure is a function together with access to its surrounding lexical environment. The function can keep accessing that environment after the outer call has returned.

function counter() {
let value = 0;
return () => {
value += 1;
return value;
};
}
const next = counter();
next(); // 1
next(); // 2

Two separate calls to counter() create two independent environments.

Change a value, keep the original

To update an item without mutating the source array, create a new array and a new object for the item that changes.

const updated = games.map(game =>
game.title === "Eclipse"
? { ...game, favorite: true }
: game
);

Unchanged objects are reused here. This is a shallow update, not a deep clone of every nested object.

